%erg v1
Title: migrate: merge archive/ into closed/ when both directories exist
Created: 2026-05-08
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-05-08T08:00Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
## Context

`erg migrate` renames `archive/` to `closed/` only when `closed/` does not
already exist. When both directories are present, the condition is false and
`archive/` is silently left behind with no warning.

This creates a silent correctness problem: the user assumes migrate cleaned up
`archive/`, but the directory remains and its tickets are invisible to
`erg check` (which only scans `tickets/` and `tickets/closed/`).

## Actions

1. When migrate finds both `archive/` and `closed/` present, move every file
   from `archive/` into `closed/`.
2. If any filename already exists in `closed/`, abort with an error naming the
   conflicting file(s) and leave both directories untouched. The user must
   resolve the conflict manually.
3. After all files are moved successfully, remove the now-empty `archive/`.
4. Print a summary line: `merged N files archive/ → closed/, removed archive/`.

The rename-only path (archive/ exists, closed/ absent) is unchanged.

## Test

```bash
# Setup: both directories present, no conflicts
mkdir -p /tmp/test-merge/tickets/{archive,closed}
echo "%erg v1" > /tmp/test-merge/tickets/archive/0001-old.erg
echo "%erg v1" > /tmp/test-merge/tickets/closed/0002-existing.erg
cd /tmp/test-merge
~/.local/bin/erg migrate
test ! -d tickets/archive  || echo "FAIL: archive/ still present"
test -f tickets/closed/0001-old.erg || echo "FAIL: file not merged"
test -f tickets/closed/0002-existing.erg || echo "FAIL: existing file lost"
echo PASS

# Conflict case
mkdir -p /tmp/test-conflict/tickets/{archive,closed}
echo "a" > /tmp/test-conflict/tickets/archive/0001-conflict.erg
echo "b" > /tmp/test-conflict/tickets/closed/0001-conflict.erg
cd /tmp/test-conflict
~/.local/bin/erg migrate && echo "FAIL: should have errored" || echo PASS
test -d tickets/archive || echo "FAIL: archive/ should be untouched on error"
```

## Exit criteria

- `erg migrate` with both `archive/` and `closed/` present moves all
  non-conflicting files and removes `archive/`.
- Name collision aborts migrate with a non-zero exit and leaves both
  directories intact.
- When only `archive/` exists (no `closed/`), the existing rename path
  is unchanged.
